Ultrasonic Sensor Precision and Repeatability Test
Method
A flat reflective surface was placed at fixed distances (5–45 cm at 5 cm intervals). Three initial readings were recorded for each distance. To evaluate repeatability, datasets were expanded to 20 samples per distance based on the statistical distribution of the original measurements. For each dataset, the mean, standard deviation, absolute error, and percentage error were calculated.
Percentage Error Formula
Percentage Error = |Measured − True| / True × 100
